    "updated_at": "2023-04-21T16:53:46Z",
    "body": "Yep, seems like a problem. This causes a renderer hang in Chromium, so it seems like there's an issue. I'll take a look.\r\n\r\nSlightly modified repo below, note that `e.newState` should be checked against `\"open\"`.\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<div id='popover1' popover>Popover 1\r\n    <div id='popover2' style=\"top:100px\" popover>Popover 2</div>\r\n    <div id='popover3' style=\"top:200px\" popover>Popover 3</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<script>\r\npopover1.showPopover(); // Show popover 1\r\npopover3.showPopover(); // Show both 1 and 3\r\npopover3.addEventListener('beforetoggle', (e) => {\r\n  if (e.newState != \"open\")\r\n    popover2.showPopover(); // When 3 closes, show 2\r\n});\r\n// Hide 1, which will first hide 3, which shows 2:\r\nsetTimeout(() => popover1.hidePopover(), 1000);\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
