    "body": "> @mfreed7 I'm not sure it's fine to allow getting a loop like that with (somewhat) innocent code... Seems like perhaps we should throw instead instead of assert?\r\n\r\nI'd be ok with that, but throw where? The natural place to detect this is right after \"hide all popovers until\", but the hide operation might be happening because of a light dismiss. In which case, there's nowhere to throw the exception, because it didn't come from a JS call. E.g. delete the `setTimeout` from the example, and just click outside all of the popovers.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
