    "updated_at": "2023-04-25T17:29:57Z",
    "body": "> Yeah, a bit on the popover would've been my solution to this fwiw (just an `isShowingOrHiding` that gets cleared when `hidePopover()` / `showPopover()` returns). Feels a bit more local, since there's no obvious place where to store the nesting (popovers can move across documents), plus conceptually you can have a very nested popup chain, and there's no reason off-hand that shouldn't work.\r\n\r\nOk, prototyping this solution seems to look ok to me. It solves the loop above, as well as this one:\r\n\r\n> Looks like this loop is same to the one in #9196.\r\n\r\nHowever, I think the \"repeat the hide all popovers until\" approach [from above](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9197#issuecomment-1518697319) is **also** needed. Otherwise in the [example above](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9197#issuecomment-1521050260), we still hit the ASSERT that p16 is at the top of the stack. It finds p17 on top. We need to repeat the \"hide all\" so that p17 gets hidden and we can complete hiding p16.",
